key_decisions.decision:
Migration 0004 uses spike 197's measured DDL for comments, unchanged:
- composite self-FK (report_id, parent_id) → comments(report_id, id) with no action clause, which is NO ACTION, backed by UNIQUE(report_id, id);
- report_id ON DELETE CASCADE;
- github_id with no action clause;
- AUTOINCREMENT ids;
- nullable removed_at;
- index comments_children(report_id, parent_id).
CASCADE on the self-FK is not used (m3). DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED is not used either: it passed every delete check, but inside an explicit transaction it accepted a cross-report row until COMMIT (spike step X), whereas NO ACTION refuses it at the INSERT.
